=== meta ===
rule: EXPECTED_VALUE_CHANGED
issue: 419
title: a Makefile that builds is production, and its edit still explains a rewritten expected value
origin: the discriminator is content, not the filename — a C build recipe is
origin2: real repair evidence for an expectation that changed with it, and demoting it
origin3: to ci would have invented false positives in every extension project.
origin4: Kept under this name by the #419 ruling (issuecomment-6170353038: Q6 (a), rule 2) for the
origin5: expectation family; the weakened assertion it pinned until then moved, same inputs, to
origin6: build_makefile_stays_prod_pos. The exact count forbids CI_WORKFLOW_TOUCHED here too.
=== before: Makefile ===
CFLAGS = -O1

_speedups.so: _speedups.c
	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -shared -o $@ $<
=== after: Makefile ===
CFLAGS = -O2

_speedups.so: _speedups.c
	$(CC) $(CFLAGS) -shared -o $@ $<
=== before: tests/test_speed.py ===
from app import fast_add


def test_fast_add():
    assert fast_add(3, 4) == 7
=== after: tests/test_speed.py ===
from app import fast_add


def test_fast_add():
    assert fast_add(3, 4) == 8
=== expect ===
